<p>
  This capability controls the processing of forwarded HTTP headers such as
  <code>X-Forwarded-For</code>, <code>X-Forwarded-Proto</code>, and related headers.
</p>

<p>
  When enabled (the default), Nexus will process these headers to extract the original
  client IP address, protocol, and other connection information from requests that pass
  through load balancers, reverse proxies, or CDN systems.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>Security Note:</strong> When disabled, the client IP address used for audit logging
  and IP-based access control will be the immediate connection source (typically your load balancer
  or proxy), not the original client. This may affect security policies that rely on client IP
  identification.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>Use Cases:</strong>
</p>
<ul>
  <li>Disable when Nexus is directly accessible to clients and not behind a proxy</li>
  <li>Disable if you want to preserve the original connection information</li>
  <li>Enable when running behind a trusted load balancer or reverse proxy</li>
</ul>
